From: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:02:39 -0300
Subject: power: supply: pmi8998_fg: fix the sign of the fallback status

pmi8998_fg_get_current() negates the PMIC's reading so that a charging
battery reports a positive current, as the power-supply ABI requires.
The status fallback, used when no charger status is known, still
treats a negative current as charging, so it reports a charging battery
as discharging and a discharging one as charging.

Compare against the converted sign.

Signed-off-by: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
@@ -346,9 +346,9 @@ static int pmi8998_fg_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN;
 				break;
 			}
-			if (temp < 0)
+			if (temp > 0)
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
-			else if (temp > 0)
+			else if (temp < 0)
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
 			else
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
-- 
